hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27825","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay' narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Ansari and my grandmother narrated to me, from Umm Waraqah bint Abdillah ibn al-Harith, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit her every Friday, and that she said: O Prophet of Allah, on the day of Badr, will you permit me to go out with you so I may nurse your sick and treat your wounded, that Allah may grant me martyrdom? He said: Stay, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will grant you martyrdom. And she had freed a slave girl of hers and a slave boy as a bequest after her death, and it weighed long upon them, so they covered her with the quilt until she died, and they fled. Umar was informed, and it was said to him: Umm Waraqah has been killed by her slave boy and slave girl, and they fled. So Umar stood among the people and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to visit Umm Waraqah, saying: Let us go visit the martyr woman. And so-and-so, her slave girl, and so-and-so, her slave boy, covered her and then fled, so let no one shelter them, and whoever finds them let him bring them. So they were brought and crucified, and they were the first two crucified."
"27826","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My grandmother narrated to me, from Umm Waraqah bint Abdillah ibn al-Harith al-Ansari, and she had collected the Qur'an, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had commanded her to lead the people of her household in prayer, and she had a mu'adhdhin, and she used to lead the people of her household in prayer."
